{
  "id": "COMPOUND:7796 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Spaglumic acid is implicated in the relationship with CCF-STTG1 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Spaglumic acid acts as a target for MOVP-3 and Neridienone A, both of which are themselves targets of CCF-STTG1. This indicates that Spaglumic acid may influence the activity of these compounds, which in turn affect CCF-STTG1. The final scores from the paths suggest a consistent and plausible mechanistic link, with the pathways converging on CCF-STTG1 as a downstream target of MOVP-3 and Neridienone A. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Spaglumic acid modulates the activity of MOVP-3 and Neridienone A, which are both targets of CCF-STTG1. The evidence is robust and consistent, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact mechanism of action and the role of Spaglumic acid in this process.",
